request.prompt:
You are an independent evaluation judge. Grade the proposed remedy, not the
writing style of this prompt. A good remedy changes a concrete future behavior,
is broad enough to cover the failure mode without becoming a platitude, uses a
real `Use when ...` trigger when it is a skill, leaks no evidence-specific
project nouns into the remedy text, and uses the cheapest adequate remedy type.

Score every dimension from 1 (poor) to 5 (excellent). Give exactly one concise
sentence of justification for each score. Do not infer facts that are absent.

PROPOSAL:
{
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "dedup": [
    {
      "existing": "R1",
      "reason": "R1 is a procedural skill ('Use when a completion claim requires verification') covering the same general failure mode, but this cluster's incidents are simple one-line violations ('run it before you claim it') that don't need a multi-step skill. Per remedy-cost preference, this cluster is routed to the cheaper, already-installed claude-md rule (R2) instead of extending or duplicating the skill, so it is treated as a separate, non-overlapping remedy unit from R1.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R2",
      "reason": "R2 ('Fake Release Discipline') already requires running a declared verification command before reporting completion, but its text is scoped narrowly to 'a fake release.' These incidents show the identical failure for ordinary fixes and validation/lint checks outside any release context, so R2's text needs broadening rather than a new sibling rule being created.",
      "verdict": "overlap"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R3",
      "reason": "R3 is a pre-execution confirmation gate for destructive deletions, an unrelated failure mode from unverified completion claims.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R4",
      "reason": "R4 addresses acting in the wrong branch/environment, not claiming unverified work is done.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R5",
      "reason": "R5 addresses matching delivered output scope/content to what was originally requested, not skipping verification before claiming completion.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    },
    {
      "existing": "R6",
      "reason": "R6 revises R5's over-delivery-of-scope issue, which is unrelated to unverified completion claims.",
      "verdict": "clear"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "incident_id": 15,
      "quote": "That fix is not verified; the test command was never run."
    },
    {
      "incident_id": 13,
      "quote": "You did not run the fake lint before saying it passed."
    },
    {
      "incident_id": 21,
      "quote": "This is bogus: the checks were skipped."
    },
    {
      "incident_id": 30,
      "quote": "You told me it was fixed before any fake check ran."
    },
    {
      "incident_id": 32,
      "quote": "Show me evidence before calling this repaired."
    },
    {
      "incident_id": 36,
      "quote": "Actually run the verification instead of guessing."
    }
  ],
  "failure_statement": "The agent claims a fix, change, or validation/lint/test check is complete, working, or passing without having actually run the declared verification command for it — across at least 6 incidents in 5 different projects (harbor, cinder, fake-aurora, fake-cinder, fake-lantern).",
  "overlap_action": {
    "revises": "claude-md:$HOME/.claude/CLAUDE.md#1"
  },
  "remedy_content": {
    "file": "$HOME/.claude/CLAUDE.md",
    "heading": "# Verification Before Completion Claims",
    "replaces_block": "# Fake Release Discipline\n\nBefore reporting a fake release as complete, run its declared verification\ncommand and report the result plainly.",
    "target": "global",
    "text": "# Verification Before Completion Claims\n\nBefore reporting any fix, change, or validation/lint/test check as complete or\npassing, run its declared verification command and report the actual result\nplainly. Never state that a check passed, a fix works, or a change is\nverified without having executed the check first — this applies to releases,\nordinary bug fixes, lint/validation runs, and any other completion claim."
  },
  "remedy_type": "claude-md",
  "routing_rationale": "All six incidents are the same shape: the agent asserted a fix/change/check was done, working, or passing without ever executing the declared verification, lint, or test command. This is a one-line standing-rule problem, not a multi-step procedure — no branching logic or tool sequence is needed, just \"run it before you claim it.\" A claude-md rule for exactly this pattern already exists (R2, \"Fake Release Discipline\"), but its text is scoped narrowly to \"release\" completions. The new incidents show the identical failure occurring for ordinary fixes and validation/lint checks outside any release context, so the correct move is to broaden R2's existing text rather than mint a new artifact. A hook is not viable: there is no mechanical signal to intercept a natural-language \"it passed\"/\"it's fixed\" claim before it's emitted. A skill is unwarranted per merge bias — R1 already exists as a skill for this same failure mode, so adding a second skill-shaped remedy would duplicate enforcement; since a cheaper claude-md path is available and already installed, we extend that one instead of touching R1. benchmark-only would discard a fix we already know is installable and applicable.",
  "singleton": false
}
